      "title": "dnp3: add filters for point indices based on the object type",
      "message": "dnp3: add filters for point indices based on the object type\n\nCurrently the DNP3 dissector uses one field (dnp3.al.index) to hold the point\nindex, shared amongst all object types. The index \"space\" is not actually\nshared between the object types, e.g. the binary input index space is logically\ndifferent from the analog input index space.\n\nThis patch implements header fields for\ndnp3.al.{bi,dbi,counter,bo,ai,ao,os}.index,\nas well as .event and .static versions of the same,\nand .cmnd indices for output objects.\n",
      "author_name": "Eric Wetzel",
      "author_email": "thewetzel@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2024-09-16T19:42:40.000-04:00",
      "committer_name": "Eric Wetzel",
      "committer_email": "thewetzel@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2025-07-20T13:22:46.000-04:00",
      "trailers": {},
      "extended_trailers": {},
      "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/commit/20626021f403b7a016129bba0c70668c74320b0b"
    },
    {
      "id": "5db2fc62dac48d1dda4eeefc06f2900ba3cb2bf9",
      "short_id": "5db2fc62",
      "created_at": "2025-07-20T13:22:45.000-04:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "cb4796e780812e98b8c83ed48b2770ef3b7267f1"
      ],
      "title": "DNP3: Handle multiple transport segments in a TCP segment",
      "message": "DNP3: Handle multiple transport segments in a TCP segment\n\nMake sure to retrieve the correct extended sequence number for\nthe particular transport segment sequence number; we can't just\nstore one for the entire frame. (It probably would also work to\njust store the previous number if nothing has been stored yet,\nas it's unlikely to have so many in one frame that the extension\nto deal with rollover would cause problems, though possibly\nwith TCO there could be quite a lot, so this is safer.)\n\nFix #14436 better.\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2024-11-06T20:38:35.000-05:00",
      "committer_name": "Eric Wetzel",
      "committer_email": "thewetzel@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2025-07-20T13:22:45.000-04:00",
