      "title": "DNP3: Only add reassembled AL packets in the FINAL fragment",
      "message": "DNP3: Only add reassembled AL packets in the FINAL fragment\n\nIt's possible to have multiple DNP3 AL fragments in the same\nTCP segment. (or UDP datagram?)\n\nInstead of checking the packet number and layer number (the last\nof which is not useful, as tcp_dissect_pdus doesn't increase the\nlayer number for each pdu), simply check if the Final bit is set.\nThis prevents adding the reassembled packet multiple times in such\ncases. (HTTP/2 has a similar approach.)\n\nAlso, if this isn't the first Data Link segment (PDU) then add a\nseparator when adding additional DNP3 transport information to\nthe Info column.\n\nFix #14436\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2024-11-06T05:19:12.000-05:00",
      "committer_name": "Eric Wetzel",
      "committer_email": "thewetzel@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2025-07-20T13:20:34.000-04:00",
      "trailers": {},
      "extended_trailers": {},
      "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/commit/2471c06447907963441cda6046297ee31f637283"
    },
    {
      "id": "fdf6bcaf2a57ca09c72dc521f13fb85be43868df",
      "short_id": "fdf6bcaf",
      "created_at": "2025-07-20T13:20:33.000-04:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "2838e0c74f7f155097d0791e615d932f46b9b254"
      ],
      "title": "DNP: Handle rollover by extending the sequence number",
      "message": "DNP: Handle rollover by extending the sequence number\n\nUse unidirectional conversations for DNP 3.0 (ignoring the port but\nusing the DNP data link address) and store the last seen sequence\nnumber, using it to extend the sequence number with cycle counting\nsimilar to done for RTP.\n\nThis likely doesn't work if frames are out of order by more than\n32 sequence numbers, but should handle most cases.\n\nFix #14437\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2024-11-05T18:45:35.000-05:00",
